# Public reading with page scripts prohibited

Demonstrated application and frontend: `9474a8121c3aadb9cacd236f005a77b54a0eafd1`.
The later product commit changes documents and evidence only. Recorded 2026-09-15,
Asia/Hong_Kong, using the Codex in-app browser at its default viewport.

The real Spring/PostgreSQL/Next.js/Caddy acceptance stack ran with fresh synthetic
repositories. A fixture-only Caddy response header set
`Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'none'; object-src 'none'` on frontend pages.
Independent HTTP inspection confirmed that header. The article contained ten script
elements, while `window.next` and `window.__next_f` remained absent. No application
script bootstrap was observed. This tests page-script prohibition by CSP, not a
browser's global JavaScript preference or all possible script-blocking extensions.

The browser opened an article from the discovery page and displayed its authored
body, title, dates and normal links. [Article screenshot](article.jpg).
The public search form submitted without hydration, returned 79 matching articles,
and its next-page link retained the query with offset 12. [Search screenshot](search.jpg).
The album's body image and two valid gallery thumbnails each loaded at natural width
320. The deliberately malformed image had width zero. Modal enlargement requires
JavaScript and is not a passing claim of this run.

Screenshots are original JPEG bytes, visually inspected and unmodified. The source
tree stayed unchanged. All fixture containers, volumes and network were removed;
no production configuration or content was touched. See [checks.json](checks.json).
